scratch/
# Stray runner output at the repository root. A run's own copy under runs/ is
# part of that run's record and is committed - verify.ps1 reads it from a fresh
# clone, so the blanket ignore silently broke verification until the negation
# below was added.
conformance-result.json
!runs/*/conformance-result.json
AzDoPAT.txt
*.pat
**/pat.txt

# Editor workspace files. Operator-local composition: which sibling repositories
# a session opens together is the operator's own business and never reaches
# anyone who clones. A TRACKED one is different - it composes the workspace of
# every clone, which is why the 'Workspace composition' assertion (d5a90b2)
# discovers via `git ls-files` and constrains tracked files only. Ignoring these
# keeps them out of that suite's scope by construction rather than by exemption.
*.code-workspace
